The main improvement opportunity is the local search: it only considers single-model *moves*, which can get stuck in local optima. Adding *swap* moves (exchanging two models between GPUs) typically lowers the max KVPR further at negligible runtime cost. I also make the search restart from the best move each iteration (already done via `break`), and consider moves from *all* GPUs, not just those exactly at the current max (helps escape ties).

